endpoint of the interval $X\\le 16$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 16) & ≈P(Y\\le 16+0.5) \\\\  & =P(Y\\le 16.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425088 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162027 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d691e3a-f9c5-5c9d-863c-533abdebb948" :knowledge-point/title "Approximating a Probability Involving a Discrete Random Variable Over an Unbounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07428db6-e061-5594-af12-24a5080b1157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(Y\\ge 9.5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425064} {:answer/id #uuid "3564fafa-635b-5b67-920a-8b89ad998edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(Y\\ge 8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425068} {:answer/id #uuid "6c01b248-edc0-5c3a-afe7-84054dabefc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(Y\\ge 7.5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425072} {:answer/id #uuid "d18d5c57-96a7-5b82-aa6b-d7f2b64a211a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(Y\\ge 8.5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425080} {:answer/id #uuid "e302ee78-c6a0-50a1-a03c-b11c2116add8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(Y\\ge 9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d18d5c57-96a7-5b82-aa6b-d7f2b64a211a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(Y\\ge 8.5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425080} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a65ee43-9417-5b75-9427-c7a5605ab37b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "baf96d37-475c-5239-92e4-1c5876314e32" :question/math-academy-id "q-132237" :question/problem "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X>8)$ can be approximated as" :question/worked-solution "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequality as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X>8)=P(X\\ge 9)\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoint of the interval $X\\ge 9$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 9) & ≈P(Y\\ge 9-0.5) \\\\  & =P(Y\\ge 8.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162679 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162026 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d41f010-e1b6-5da8-ab37-c584d84dd5b6" :knowledge-point/title "Approximating a Probability Involving a Discrete Random Variable Over an Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01d60f05-c149-5def-b6ca-6ac37c02ecce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(0.5\\le Y\\le 4.5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425063} {:answer/id #uuid "07e95014-9cde-5766-9827-921ed2bfc5e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(1.5\\le Y\\le 5.5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425065} {:answer/id #uuid "36c79b55-d3d7-513c-bea5-e6b4e2f37fb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(0\\le Y\\le 6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425069} {:answer/id #uuid "b729172a-2775-5903-9a85-cf462a6f041e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(1.5\\le Y\\le 4.5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425077} {:answer/id #uuid "ed9cf813-6d76-5f99-881d-b8d9cc313502" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(1\\le Y\\le 5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b729172a-2775-5903-9a85-cf462a6f041e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(1.5\\le Y\\le 4.5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425077} :answer-field/id #uuid "24b4f3dd-61dd-5644-bb2d-47da345a9a46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a3bc8c1-8950-5912-8763-bb2c4cf11d4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96134" :question/problem "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(1<X<5)$ can be approximated as" :question/worked-solution "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequalities as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X<5) & =P(2\\le X\\le 4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoints of the interval $2\\le X\\le 4$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le X\\le 4) & ≈P(2-0.5\\le Y\\le 4+0.5) \\\\  & =P(1.5\\le Y\\le 4.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425086 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162025 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7be1caf7-728f-5c51-b3da-64f3f7ff6fa9" :knowledge-point/title "Approximating a Probability Involving a Discrete Random Variable at a Single Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "200fbb3c-40ed-5f05-be1e-0229439b9ea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(5\\le Y\\le 5.5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425066} {:answer/id #uuid "aea03d54-47ff-5704-91a4-d89cf538b880" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(5\\le Y\\le 6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425075} {:answer/id #uuid "b4a26668-5f4b-5cc5-bd3b-0f6627b55524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(4.5\\le Y\\le 5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425076} {:a